  "notes": [
    "The green module proves two algebraic identities: the finite-list reverse-Horner expression equals evaluation of the selected ascending-monomial semantic polynomial, and the boundary forward fold equals the sum of that polynomial's evaluations at 0 and 1.",
    "The generic finite-list Horner induction reuses the proof route of the older SourceMixing theorem but is stated locally to avoid its larger generated-module imports.",
